{{!
    @template local_awareness/manage/empty

    Empty state for the notice list. Rendered by the table itself rather than by the page around
    it, because an AJAX refresh replaces the table's HTML and nothing else — an empty state living
    outside would keep showing the previous answer.

    Two shapes, deliberately different: a site with no notices at all is invited to create one, and
    a filter that matched nothing is offered a way back out instead.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * message (string) - what happened
    * showcreate (bool) - offer the create-notice call to action
    * createurl (string) - where that goes
    * createlabel (string) - its label
    * showclear (bool) - offer to clear the filters
    * clearlabel (string) - its label

    @copyright  2026 Anderson Blaine
    @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later

    Example context (json):
    {
        "message": "No notices match these filters.",
        "showclear": true,
        "clearlabel": "Clear filters"
    }
}}
<div class="local-awareness-empty" data-region="la-empty">
    <p class="mb-3">{{message}}</p>
    {{#showcreate}}
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{createurl}}">{{createlabel}}</a>
    {{/showcreate}}
    {{#showclear}}
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" data-action="clear-filters">{{clearlabel}}</button>
    {{/showclear}}
</div>
